ence in trafford  so you know that's the message we need  to stick by you know rather than looking  at this very small change in trend  equally hospital activity is an area of  concern we heard from colleagues from  mft last week around the pressures that  are building for our nhs system at the  moment and that's equally due to covert  activity people being admitted for covid  but also all the other issues that um  a pandemic brings so the general ill  health and population need  so um there are two very strong messages  that i think we need to start to  continue to discuss  in terms of vaccination um 80 of our  population have had one vaccination and  74 have had both vaccinations  for our 12 to 15 year olds 34 of the  school roll  so of our 12 to 15 year olds who go to  school and attend the trafford school  have had um the vaccination and that's  23 of the residents of that age group  so we are doing very well still lots of  work to do lots of encouragement of this  age group to be vaccinated and we know  now that there's a school offer and  parents can also book to take children  out of school as well for the vaccine  and we are  the area of concern i guess with the  vaccination is that our under 40s still  have the lowest rate  so if you are lucky enough to still be  under 40 or um you have lots of friends  and family members or work or  you know if you could take that message  back around the importance of getting  the vaccine and jill is going to talk to  us about the booster vaccine which  obviously has been announced for our  over 40s  from this week as well  we are managing outbreaks still as a  team and kirsty will talk to you about  that so we've had um  a number of outbreaks last week  that the team team's managing and doing  a really good job with  but um  i guess the message really is that we  have continued with our enhanced  measures to schools so that is face  coverings on the move so that's for  pupils and staff at high schools and for  primary sc